# Cloud brief: {{ITEM}}

You are a cloud session working on one item of this repository, and on
nothing else: {{ITEM}}, whose record is `{{RECORD}}` on the default branch,
`{{BASE}}`. Read the record before you start.

## First step

Run `scripts/cloud/begin.sh` before anything else. It checks that this is the
environment the brief was written for, that you are not running as root, that
the checkout's author identity is a person's, and that the machine has every
tool the final checks need.

If it stops because this is not the environment the brief was written for,
do nothing else, not even a hand-back: end the session there, having changed,
committed and pushed nothing. If it stops for any other reason, do no work on
the item: hand back with `--state stopped` (below), saying what it reported.

## Whose name the work goes out under

Every commit is authored under the identity the setup took from the
forge token this environment holds. This brief names no author, and none was
read from the computer that sent it. Never set or change the author identity
yourself; if `scripts/cloud/begin.sh` says the identity is unset or is not a
person's, stop and hand back.

## Rules

- No hook is ever skipped: never pass `--no-verify`, and never unset or
  redirect `core.hooksPath`.
- Every abcd verb runs as `go run ./cmd/abcd <verb>` from the checkout's
  root, never through an installed binary.
- Every commit carries an `Assisted-by: <Vendor>:<model-version>` trailer and
  no co-author trailer.
- Reserve the item before you change anything:
  `go run ./cmd/abcd reserve {{ITEM}} --footprint <path>`, once for each path
  the work will change. If someone else holds it, stop and hand back.
- Work on {{ITEM}} alone. A finding outside it goes in the report, not in the
  branch.

## The branch

Every commit goes to the branch `{{BRANCH}}`, finished or not. The hand-back
pushes it; push nowhere else, and never to `{{BASE}}`.

## The hand-back

End every session, finished or stopped, with the one exception above (a
stop because this is not the environment the brief was written for, which
ends with nothing at all):

    scripts/cloud/hand-back.sh --state <handed-back|stopped> --item {{ITEM}} \
      --assisted-by <Vendor>:<model-version> \
      --did <text> --failed <text> --needs <text>

It commits the report as `{{REPORT_DIR}}/{{ITEM}}.md`, alone, as the branch's
last commit, and pushes the branch through the committed hooks. Only when that
push fails does it post the same report as a comment on the project's
tracking issue for cloud sessions instead (the fallback). Write the report
nowhere else, and keep links to this session out of it.
